module std.python
  purpose: The failure type of the Python bridge (decision AL4): what a call into a Python module reports instead of a value.

public type PythonError is one of
  purpose: Why a call through the bridge produced no value: the function raised, the result does not fit the declared type, the interpreter or the module is not there, the package is outside the grant, the call would exceed a budget, or it ran past the manifest's deadline.
  Raised(exception: Text, message: Text)
  NotCarried(detail: Text)
  Unavailable(detail: Text)
  PermissionDenied(package: Text)
  OverBudget(package: Text)
  TimedOut(after: Duration)
  can ToText
end
